eefacm@gmail.com wrote:
> What are the appropriate steps to take after losing track of one's
> pet?

depends on the size of the pet. In the case of dogs or cats it is: tame 
a new one. In the case of carnivorous pets it should be a quick 
magic-whistling run up the stairs (tameness degrades by 1 point/150 
turns, so you have slightly less than 3000 turns to find it), and in the 
case of a lich it might even be a scroll of genocide.

> Sometimes, though, they're well and truly gone.  I just lost my dog on
> my way up from Mine's End, and I couldn't find him after redescending
> all the way to the bottom.  The possibilities that occur to me are:
> 
> *  Killed by a physical trap.

unfortunately as a dog it caried no items and the corpse might have 
rotted away, so you will never be sure.

> *  Stepped on a level teleport trap.

big fun. This means it can be anywhere between level 1 and mineend 
(IIRC). Be sure to bring your magic whistle or blessed eucalypthos leaf.

> *  Stepped on a polymorph trap.

easy, since it retains the name.

> The last one is a distinct possibility in this case, since I stepped
> on a such a trap myself, turning into a nalfeshnee (with the nice
> effect of giving me three new pets: two other nalfeshnee and a horned
> devil).  But I've scanned all of the lower levels with my telepathy,
> and no monsters are identified as the name I gave the dog, which I
> hazily remember ought to be the case.

it may have polymorphed into a mindless monster.

> and if the dog was teleported to another level I imagine it'll
> probably go feral before I find it.  Should I just give it up for
> lost?

dogs in Nethack are cannon fodder. Just get yourself a new one by 
throwing a corpse or fortune cookie at it.

> Unrelated question:  Excalibur was blasting me for a while every time
> I picked it up, and I couldn't figure out why.  The wiki says that
> should happen only in case of conflicting alignment, but I was always
> Lawful when it happened.

maybe not lawful enough?

>  Later, I remembered:  Oh yeah, I was a demon
> for a while.  Is that the reason?

IDHTSIFOM mut it seams reasonable, especially since you can't pray as a 
lawful polymorphed into a demon.

